`functools.lru_cache` is a decorator used for memoization. It stores the results of expensive function calls and returns the cached result when the same inputs occur again. This avoids recomputing values. "LRU" stands for "Least Recently Used," meaning it discards the least recently used items when the cache reaches its maximum size.

Example:
```python
from functools import lru_cache

@lru_cache(maxsize=128) # Cache up to 128 distinct calls
def fibonacci(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    return fibonacci(n-1) + fibonacci(n-2)
```
